# Project Scope (starter pack template)

This rule complements the generic `agent-flow.mdc` with project-specific scope.
Every agent run loads both: the generic pipeline rules AND this rule.

> **Edit this file** before installing the pack to reflect your project's
> actual stack, paths, and build commands. The placeholders below are
> illustrative, not real.

## Project context

All agents run in this repo only.

**Tech stack** _(EDIT — list what your project actually uses)_:

- Frontend: Angular 18 / Angular 19 / React / Vue 3 — pick what applies
- Backend: Java 17+ + Spring Boot 3.x
- Build: Maven or Gradle (backend), npm + Vite or Angular CLI (frontend)

**Primary paths** _(EDIT)_:

- `frontend/src/` — frontend source
- `backend/src/main/java/` — Java backend source
- `backend/src/test/java/` — backend tests

## Build safety

**NEVER run destructive targets.** Examples — adapt to your project:

- Anything that drops or recreates the database
- Production deploy commands (`./deploy.sh prod`, `mvn deploy -P prod`, etc.)
- `git push --force` to shared branches
- `npm publish` or `mvn deploy` to public registries

## Allowed build commands

_(EDIT — fill in your project's real commands)_

- **Surgeon (backend, fast feedback):** `mvn -pl backend compile`
- **Surgeon (frontend, fast feedback):** `cd frontend && npm run build:dev`
- **Surgeon (full per-task verification):** `mvn verify` (backend) or `npm run build` (frontend)
- **Review (final gate):** `mvn clean verify && cd frontend && npm run build`
- **Tests:** `mvn test` (backend), `npm test` (frontend)

## Ticket prefix

Ticket prefixes are extracted from the trigger at runtime — no whitelist needed.
`@orchestrator.md Work on PROJ-1234` → prefix `PROJ`.

Branch and base-branch conventions live in `pipeline.starter.yaml`
under `runtime.branching`:

- `runtime.branching.prefix_story` — e.g. `"feature/"`
- `runtime.branching.prefix_bug`   — e.g. `"fix/"`
- `runtime.branching.base_branch`  — e.g. `"main"` or `"develop"`

## Standing context

Team boundaries, active migrations, and reference implementations that
shift over time live in `contexts/project-context.md`, NOT here. This file
is the stable scope; `project-context.md` is the living knowledge base.
